From: Horizon authors <>
Subject: [PATCH] Restore new-game partner care before the opening

The title prepares a new SavegamePayload, including the configured starting
age, but only Continue calls initializeLoadedMap to copy its partner care to
the live state. The USA initializePartner leaves age and several care counters
alone. A cold boot therefore starts at zero days and a New Game after returning
to the title can inherit the preceding partner's age.

Restore the new payload's care before the opening. Partner initialization still
sets species-dependent care and birth values; Continue keeps its saved care.
---
 src/main/main.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main/main.c b/src/main/main.c
--- a/src/main/main.c
+++ b/src/main/main.c
@@ -3520,6 +3520,10 @@ void main(void)
 	cheats_loaded:
 		switch (MAIN_STATE) {
 		case 0:
+			/* The title prepared a new payload. Restore its care before the
+			 * opening; initializePartner does not reset age on USA builds. */
+			PARTNER_PARA = SAVED_STATE.partnerPara;
+
 			newGameScene();
 			finalizeMusic();
 			playMovie(1, 1);
